WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
NASA satellites watched fire activity for decades.
The record changes when the sensor changes.

00:05.000 --> 00:15.000
MODIS and VIIRS are different native measurements.
FireAtlas keeps both and groups them once per UTC day on a common 1 km grid.

00:15.000 --> 00:35.000
The calendar shows its evidence state.
Documented gaps are estimates or unknown, never silent zeros.

00:35.000 --> 00:50.000
Open the source record behind one day.
UTC time, confidence, product version, FRP, notices, and hashes remain inspectable.

00:50.000 --> 01:05.000
The same controls show another fire regime.
Official context is separate; thermal detections do not identify cause.

01:05.000 --> 01:20.000
A checked match is visible before the claim.
Native granules and FIRMS rows are counted; independent review remains pending.

01:20.000 --> 01:30.000
Value, state, version, hash, and limit stay in one evidence card.
Every claim remains traceable.
